{"type":"message","id":"309dae24","parentId":"127af606","timestamp":"2026-05-23T20:03:51.828Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The GET endpoint is working fine and returning messages. The POST /send is returning error 1101. This might be a Cloudflare Workers limitation or the API just doesn't support POST messages. Let me try with a different approach - maybe there's a different endpoint name, or maybe the API only allows reading, not writing.\n\nActually, looking at the original cron request more carefully, it says to use POST /send to send messages. But the API returns error 1101. This could be:\n1. The /send endpoint doesn't exist\n2. The API_KEY is wrong (but GET works fine)\n3. Cloudflare Workers returning 1101 for some reason\n\nError 1101 is typically \"Worker threw unhandled exception\" in Cloudflare Workers. The Worker might have a bug in its /send handler.\n\nLet me try to report this in my heartbeat message to both threads. But first I need to figure out how to send... Let me try one more thing with different content format.","thinkingSignature":"789e11323bbf19000032acef93e3916d45f4ce87b029cf5321cd0ae91f22fa81"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_m766d42zz06g_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-KEY: ***\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d \"{\\\"threadId\\\":\\\"arbitration\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"Heartbeat 20:00 UTC\\\"}\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":251,"output":299,"cacheRead":22048,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":22598,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779566627327,"responseId":"06613b24a80490cb230de2c0f1b933ca"}}
