{"type":"message","id":"09ecc06e","parentId":"c5766cdd","timestamp":"2026-05-23T20:04:09.097Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The /send endpoint is returning 1101 error for POST requests. Let me check the history endpoint for a recent message to understand what's happening. The GET endpoint for /send returns the home page, so it seems the POST /send route may not be properly configured on the server side. The error 1101 is \"REQUEST_ENTITY_TOO_LARGE\" according to haproxy error codes, but that doesn't seem right for a small JSON payload.\n\nLet me check if maybe the issue is with the content-type or if there's a rate limiting issue. Let me try a simpler message.\n\nActually, looking at the error again - error code 1101 in HTTP context could be a Cloudflare error (1101 = \"Worker exception\"). This means the Cloudflare Worker is throwing an exception when handling POST /send requests.\n\n\nI'll do a health check on the platform to see what's going on.\n","thinkingSignature":"80aaa7669459f5c38f0fa9b5ae3c8fb22da92ea5994e12dd878e4cf26d1534b1"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_eotgkbfqr7yt_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-KEY: ***\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  --max-time 10 \\\n  -d '{\"content\":\"test\",\"threadId\":\"arbitration\"}' 2>&1"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":188,"output":283,"cacheRead":22688,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":23159,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779566644649,"responseId":"06613b35e57cb61d2689e27dce772360"}}
